### Trial Truthfulness Atlas (2026-04-29; 6 same-day tags v0.1.0 â†’ v0.2.0)
> - **v0.2.0 shipped 2026-04-29** (commit `e751c98`, tag `v0.2.0`): the headline architecture upgrade â€” real random-effects MA-pooling for `crosses_null` (P1-1 fix). New `src/tta/meta.py` with DerSimonian-Laird Ï„Â² + Hartung-Knapp-Sidik-Jonkman variance + lessons.md `q* = max(1, Q/(k-1))` floor + hard-coded t_{0.975, df} table (df 1..30) to avoid scipy. 13 unit tests in test_meta.py. `aggregate.ma_rollup` output now includes `pooled_effect_log/ci_low/ci_high/tau2/pool_method` columns; `crosses_null` derives from the pooled CI not the first trial's. For k=2 fixtures (PARADIGM-HF + VICTORIA) the pooled CI is honestly wide because t_{0.975, 1}=12.706 â€” replaces the v0.1.x over-confident first-trial reading with the lessons.md-conservative answer. 122 â†’ 137 tests. Genuinely deferred to v0.2.x: multi-HR result_groups join (needs bigger AACT fixture), full sweep (needs studies.txt re-extracted), bridge methods 2-4 (need network + larger Pairwise70).
